<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Iseo</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sebino</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lake Iseo is a lake in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, lying between the provinces of Bergamo and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brescia">Brescia</a> and fed and drained by the Oglio river. Its island of Monte Isola is one of the largest lake islands in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. The lake shores, with the Franciacorta wine district to the south, belonged to Brescia's territory in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lake-iseo.jpg" alt="Lake Iseo" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Palabras. Giorces uploads. · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LagoIseo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
